Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:09:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] daemon: CA speech flag 0x02 ducks like 0x01

Per the AAP notes 01/02 both mean the wearer is speaking and 03 means stopped; 02 used to fall through to the voice-ended path.
---
 daemon/media/mediacontroller.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/daemon/media/mediacontroller.cpp b/daemon/media/mediacontroller.cpp
index 7e209ec..d5e8f33 100644
--- a/daemon/media/mediacontroller.cpp
+++ b/daemon/media/mediacontroller.cpp
@@ -173,6 +173,7 @@ void MediaController::handleConversationalAwareness(const QByteArray &data) {
 
     switch (flag) {
     case 0x01:
+    case 0x02:
         LOG_INFO("Conversational awareness event: voice detected");
 
         if (initialVolume == -1 && isActiveOutputDeviceAirPods()) {
